00:02:33.159 --> 00:02:37.349
of words themselves, especially the words
that may have attracted you to this program,

00:02:37.349 --> 00:02:44.300
such as neurons, self, memory. What is memory?
Soul, soul. You must have thought about that

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:51.519
emotion. Mind. What is the mind? Consciousness.
Scientists and philosophers have been pointing

00:02:51.519 --> 00:02:55.840
out for a long time that just because we've
got a word for something doesn't necessarily

00:02:55.840 --> 00:03:00.569
mean there's anything there, including self,
consciousness, for example. We may feel we

00:03:00.569 --> 00:03:06.990
know what the word means and use it freely
and even use it very well. But, it doesn't

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:12.440
necessarily mean that there's anything there.
But each word has been evolving in its usage

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:18.819
for centuries and our human ability to constantly
change and create their meanings. Well we

00:03:18.819 --> 00:03:25.019
have to keep that in mind, so to speak. We
have to constantly remind our- so to speak,

00:03:25.019 --> 00:03:29.850
we have to remind ourselves about the fact
that words themselves don't necessarily tell

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:38.290
us about something that's there. As our panelists
use words here, this evening, and gestures,

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:44.120
and emotions, probably to try to enlighten
